54	 * not leak memory through long-lived thread references.
55	 * <p>
56	 * Before HADOOP-18091 the active span of each thread was stored in a
57	 * {@code ThreadLocal}; as the span referenced the audit manager, and
58	 * hence the auditor and the filesystem, nothing was ever released for
59	 * threads in long-lived thread pools.
60	 * <p>
61	 * The leak is recreated here by creating a long sequence of audit
62	 * managers whose auditors and spans allocate a lot of memory, and
63	 * using them from a long-lived thread pool. On the original code this
64	 * would trigger an OOM; with the weak reference map the spans are
65	 * released once garbage collection takes place.
66	 */
